    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2024-june/q2",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:120mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2024-june/q02-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Speed-time graph: speed (m s^-1) against t (s). Speed rises in a straight line from 0 at t = 0 to 10 at t = 4, stays at 10 until t = 18, then falls in a straight line to U at t = 24. Dashed lines mark t = 4, t = 18, speed U and t = 24.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a speed-time graph for a model of the motion of an athlete running a <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{200\\,m}\"></span> race in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"24\\,\\mathrm s\"></span>.</p><p>The athlete</p><ul><li>starts from rest at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\"></span> and accelerates at a constant rate, reaching a speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\"></span></li><li>then moves at a constant speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=18\"></span></li><li>then decelerates at a constant rate from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=18\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=24\"></span>, crossing the finishing line with speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}\"></span></li></ul><p>Using the model,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>find the acceleration of the athlete during the first <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\,\\mathrm s\"></span> of the race, stating the units of your answer, <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>find the distance covered by the athlete during the first <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"18\\,\\mathrm s\"></span> of the race, <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
