    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-32-2024-june/q6",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:90mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-32-2024-june/q05-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 5. A uniform rod AB rests with end A on horizontal ground, inclined at angle theta to the ground, touching a small peg P at point C, with AC = 1.5a marked by a double-headed arrow along the rod.\"></figure><p>Figure 5 shows a uniform rod <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span> of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span> and length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2a\"></span>.</p><ul><li>the rod has its end <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> on rough horizontal ground</li><li>the rod rests in equilibrium against a small smooth fixed horizontal peg <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span></li><li>the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> on the rod, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC=1.5a\"></span>, is the point of contact between the rod and the peg</li><li>the rod is at an angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> to the ground, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{4}{3}\"></span></li></ul><p>The rod lies in a vertical plane perpendicular to the peg.</p><p>The magnitude of the normal reaction of the peg on the rod at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S=\\dfrac{2}{5}Mg\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The coefficient of friction between the rod and the ground is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span>.</p><p>Given that the rod is in limiting equilibrium,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
